    // Bugs

    "bugs.beetle.name": "Stag Beetle",
    "bugs.beetle.scientific": "Lucanidae",
    "bugs.beetle.description": "Their mandibles grow over the course of their lifetime to the length of their body. Males wrestle one-another for females, food, and territory. Despite their size, they remain capable flyers.",

    "bugs.butterfly.name": "Monarch Butterfly",
    "bugs.butterfly.scientific": "Danaus plexippus",
    "bugs.butterfly.description": "Renowned for their continental migration patterns, species are found wherever their preferred food grows, as well as at various points along their migratory routes. Scales take from a palette of orange, white, and blue.",

    "bugs.wasp.name": "Paper Wasp",
    "bugs.wasp.scientific": "Vespidae",
    "bugs.wasp.description": "As with bees, a lone queen founds a nest, spawning female workers to grow her brood. An adult wasp can't feed on solid matter; her mandibles are mainly for pulping wood fiber into paper. She subsists on nectar and feeds processed insects to her larvae.",

    "bugs.grasshopper.name": "Grasshopper",
    "bugs.grasshopper.scientific": "Acrididae",
    "bugs.grasshopper.description": "Especially prehistoric insects with powerful wings and spurred hindlegs. May transform into locusts in adverse conditions. Infamous competition for crops such as grains and herbs.",

    "bugs.mantis.name": "Orchid Mantis",
    "bugs.mantis.scientific": "Hymenopus coronatus",
    "bugs.mantis.description": "Beautiful predators with toothed legs and powerful mandibles. Can change their camouflage at will, ambushing pollinating insects before they can react.\n\nFemales grow to twice the size of males, eating them after mating ..!",

    "bugs.louse.name": "Woodlouse",
    "bugs.louse.scientific": "Porcellionidae",
    "bugs.louse.description": "Nocturnal detritivores that decompose wood, manure, and other plant matter. Descended from marine isopods, they prefer damp habitats.\n\nVery cute given the number of legs.",

    "bugs.centipede.name": "Centipede",
    "bugs.centipede.scientific": "Scolopendridae",
    "bugs.centipede.description": "Aggressive predator capable of subduing disproportionately-large prey with its envenomed pincer-like forelimbs, even though mostly blind. Can live for up to 10 years in an ideal environment, growing additional legs with every moult.\n\nExtremely uncute. May take a lot of pins.",

    "bugs.moth.name": "Moon Moth",
    "bugs.moth.scientific": "Actias luna",
    "bugs.moth.description": "Large silk moth with a ghostly scale. Larvae thrive on cherry and maple trees in the region, adults survive only on larval energy stores.\n\nRelative of Actias artemis. Cute!",

    "bugs.termite.name": "Termite",
    "bugs.termite.scientific": "Rhinotermitidae",
    "bugs.termite.description": "Feeds on exposed wood, breeds underground in vast colonies millions-strong. Divided into a dimorphic social system, workers and soldiers support eachother under a king and queen.\n\nI hope there's no more where this came from..",

    "bugs.ladybug.name": "Ladybird",
    "bugs.ladybug.scientific": "Coccinellidae",
    "bugs.ladybug.description": "Pretty guardians of the rose garden! Deceptively effective predators of small garden pests. Habitats are vast due to prolific breeding and individual range.\nSpecies within this family come in a wide range of colours and patterns.\n\nMako won't be happy if I pin this one.",

    "bugs.dragonfly.name": "Dragonfly",
    "bugs.dragonfly.scientific": "Libellulidae",
    "bugs.dragonfly.description": "Agile aerial aces with precise flight and sight. Preferred habitats are near vegetated freshwater bodies such as lakes, rivers, and wetlands. Hatchling nymphs develop underwater for several years before emerging to breed and perish.\n\nIconic features of traditional paintings.",

    "bugs.scarab.name": "Jewel Scarab",
    "bugs.scarab.scientific": "Scarabaeidae",
    "bugs.scarab.description": "Rarely-seen beetles with an iridescent carapace, only found in mountainous coniferous forests. Their metallic sheen comes from many layers of uniquely-coloured reflective chitin. Different species have a huge variety of colours!",

    // Dialogue

    "chicken.fight.1": "Hey! Stop that!",
    "chicken.fight.2": "Not again...",
    "chicken.fight.3": "What are you doing?!",
    "chicken.fight.4": "Leave the chickens alone!",
    "chicken.fight.5": "Oh no...",
    "chicken.fight.6": "{{farmer}}?!",

    "rei.test": "DialoguePicker Rei default text#$b#$action Custom_Hikawa_DialogueEffects wave 3.5 1#$b#Second line is wavy#$e#$action Custom_Hikawa_DialogueEffects shake 2#$b#Reset dialogue is shaky#$b#$action Custom_Hikawa_DialogueEffects reset#$b#Next one",
    "rei.chat.1": "You should come get your fortune told sometime.#$b#I'm always right <",
    "rei.chat.2": "You should watch the sunset from the shrine sometime. You can see it across the mountains.#$e#It's really something special seeing clouds glow like pink cherry trees.",
    "rei.chat.3": "I hope you don't mind being around a cemetery.#$b#The north side of the hill has been a sacred burial place for much, much longer than my family's lived here.#$e#Maybe one day we'll rest here, too.",
    "rei.chat.4": "Being so high up here, we get a whole lot of wind.#$e#A few years ago, the roof for the hall got blown in and collapsed.#$b#Grandpa's been fixing it since. He's got all the tiles back up, but the rafters inside are still broken.#$e#Or so he says.",
    "rei.chat.5": "It gets dark at the shrine pretty early.#$b#We've only got the lanterns outside, so don't stay out too late.",
    "rei.chat.6": "Don't bother the chickens. They don't like strangers.#$e#Don't say I didn't warn you.",
    "rei.chat.7": "There's a lot of spirits that call the shrine their home.#$b#It's not the last resting place for all of them. Sometimes they're just resting.",
    "rei.chat.8": "It's soothing watching the stars come out at night. Knowing they've been watching over you all day.#$b#But you couldn't tell anything was there at all.",
    "rei.chat.9": "I make sure to light the lanterns around the cemetery each night.#$b#It's just another duty in the day, but I'm sure it means a lot to someone.",
    "rei.chat.10": "Just before summer ends and colder weather comes in, we put together a bonfire and share a moment with the dead.#$b#You can join in if you like. There'll be food!#$e#.. Or whatever's left after Ami finds it.",
    "rei.chat.11": "It's a lot of work keeping this old shrine from falling apart.#$b#The closer you live to nature, the more you feel the elements are against you.#$e#I'm glad it's not just grandpa and me here.",
    "rei.chat.12": "Do you believe in ghosts, @?#$e#.. No, you don't seem like the type.",
    "rei.chat.13": "I've given up on styling my hair at home. One gust of wind and it's ruined.#$b#We get a lot of wind here...",
    "rei.chat.14": "The lanterns here gather wandering spirits like moths.#$b#Even if it's a lonely old hill for the living, it's lively enough for some others.",
    "rei.chat.15": "We keep crows here. It's said they ward away evil.#$b#Phobos and Deimos are ours, the rest come and go as they choose.#$e#They don't give you any trouble, do they?",
    "rei.chat.16": "How's your old farmhouse, @?#$b#If you think your place is drafty, come visit ours for a while.#$b#Hope you're not too used to living in the city.",
    "rei.chat.17": "If you've got some spare time, you could pick up the broom for a while.#$b#Your hands are probably like leather from working the farm.",
    "rei.chat.18": "I wish our friends would visit more often...#$b#When you live this far from the city, it's easy to get lonely.#$e#Don't you have any city friends you left behind?",
    "rei.chat.19": "There's another little graveyard in town too, you know. I think it's mostly for the families around there.",
    "rei.chat.20": "%Rei's ignoring you. Probably.",
    "rei.chat.21": "There's 44 stone steps leading up to the shrine. It doesn't sound like a lot until you've got to go back again.",
    "rei.chat.22": "Grandpa's getting a little old these days. I'm sure it's getting harder for him to get around.#$b#Keep an eye on him for me, okay?",
    "rei.chat.23": ".. Is that a ghostly hand on your shoulder ..?",
    "rei.chat.24": "The stars weren't in harmony last night.#$b#Tonight doesn't seem any better...",
    "rei.chat.25": "Don't bother me today.#$e#...#$e#Get a clue.",
    "rei.chat.26": "It's hard avoiding a tan around here. I wear more sunscreen than makeup.#$e#That's kinda sad, actually.",
    "rei.chat.27": "Try not to bug Ami when she's studying.#$e#Yes, I know she's always studying..",
    "rei.chat.28": "You start to miss school when it's over. I got used to seeing the same people everyday..#$b#Makes me feel empty losing them to go live on a mountain in the middle of nowhere.#$e#Life was simple in school.#$b#It was stressful, too, but still..",
    "rei.chat.29": "I wonder when Ami's going back to the city for good.#$b#I love having someone else around, but.. she can't stay forever, right?",
    "rei.chat.30": "Watch your step around the shrine at night.#$b#There's loose tiles and rocks everywhere, you can barely see them in the dark.#$e#I broke a toe kicking a stupid brick one night.#$b#Laugh if up! It'll happen to you, too.",
    "rei.chat.31": "Most of the shrine was built from cherry trees felled years ago.#$b#Since cherry wood burns so easily, it's been rebuilt a few times in its history.#$e#.. No, I wasn't even here last time.",
    "rei.chat.32": "Grandpa was one of the workmen the last time the shrine needed some building done. He's got a lot of experience with woodwork.#$b#It's been a hobby of his for as long as I can remember. Pretty much all the furniture at home is his work.#$e#These days people just order their homewares online. I don't know when he last had an order...",
    "rei.chat.33": "I haven't seen Grandpa put together any new furniture in a while, but he always seems to be working on something.#$b#Wonder what he's up to now.",
    "rei.chat.34": "Cherry Hill Shrine was once a place of worship for an old god of fire.#$b#The legend's long since forgotten, but the shrine survives. Now it's a place of remembrance for lost spirits.#$e#Fire hasn't left the shrine over the years, though.#$b#Even when the great hall burned down, we kept the embers burning. The same fire lives on in the hall now.",
    "rei.chat.35": "Wow, you.. really smell.#$b#Use a lot of manure on the farm, huh?",
    "rei.chat.36": "Don't walk around the house in those boots. I don't even want to think what you've stepped in on the way here.",
    "rei.chat.37": "No, we don't make 'chewed sake' here. Don't even ask for it.",
    "rei.chat.38": "We used to hold services and stuff in the small hall. The one with the pointed roof.#$b#When the roof blew in we had to give it up, though. Grandpa never did finish mending it.",
    "rei.chat.39": "You can visit the cemetery if you like. Take a walk around.#$b#There's a lot of history marked in stone and wood. Names no longer spoken, people lost far from home, maybe the last branch of a family tree. Names I've never seen a living soul use.#$e#Sometimes I wonder if my grave will watch the sunset over the hills here, too.",
    "rei.chat.40": "We do purification rites before dawn's first light.#$b#You can come along if you're ever awake early enough.",
    "rei.chat.41": "We sell all sorts of things at the shop. Drop in sometime and have a look around.",
    "rei.chat.42": "If you'd like to make an offering at the shrine, drop some coins into the box at the great hall.#$b#Who knows? Maybe the spirits will look kindly on a donation.#$e#If nothing else it'll help pay for a new roof.",
    "rei.chat.43": "The ropes hanging around the shrine aren't for decoration. They're tied here to bind us to the world of spirits.#$b#They're unbelievably heavy, too. It'd be easier picking up the front gate than lifting one of these.",
    "rei.chat.44": "There's a special kind of magic in looking through your window in the spring and seeing flower petals fall like rain.#$b#It's like living in a storybook. I'll never get tired of it.",
    "rei.chat.45": "I look forward to autumn every year. Not just for the festivals, but the colours.#$b#Seeing the shrine all lit up in red and gold, leaves drifting through the air like embers..#$b#Maybe we'll even wrap up the bonfire without something catching fire.",
    "rei.chat.46": "",
    "rei.chat.": "",

    "ami.test": "DialoguePicker Ami default text",
    "ami.chat.1": "Hi..",
    "ami.chat.2": "It's hard to see the stars at night, but the cool air's still perfectly enjoyable.#$e#It's still much easier here than in the city. Without light pollution, you can make out some of the constellations in the sky.",
    "ami.chat.3": ".. What? Sorry, I'm in the middle of some test papers.",
    "ami.chat.4": ".. These notes? Oh, they aren't mine.#$b#I'm leading a study group for anatomy! I can't wait for class to start.#$e#How many semesters away is it now ..?",
    "ami.chat.5": "Cherry Hill isn't a great place to be if you've any allergies. Flowers, pollen, dust, smoke, cat hair..#$e#If you come out in a rash, be sure to let me know.#$b#It'd be interesting to compare your reaction with a textbook case.",
    "ami.chat.6": "Studying remote isn't so bad, really.#$b#On the one hand, I'm surrounded by the most beautiful, peaceful landscape..#$b#On the other, there's not a cram school around for miles..",
    "ami.chat.7": "My laptop? It's not new, I've had it for years.#$b#.. Where did I get it? Um..",
    "ami.chat.8": "It's wonderful how elements in nature provide for one-another.#$b#The endless exchange of carbon dioxide, oxygen, and matter between plants and animals, bacterial fixation of nitrogen and sulfur from air to earth...#$e#I'm sure you've worked hard to determine the ideal conditions for your soil culture. That's very admirable.",
    "ami.chat.9": "Living here after growing up in the city is a real culture shock. Rei's family lives without so much as a hairdryer.#$b#Having to do the dishes by hand really cuts into my study time.",
    "ami.chat.10": "When I first met Rei, she always appeared so neat and formal. You couldn't imagine her doing the chores she has to do at the shrine.#$b#Still, I don't think most people would look quite so elegant holding a broom.",
    "ami.chat.11": "The shrine must have looked very different when it was first constructed.#$b#All the rooftops here are copper, meaning their dazzling blue colour developed over time as a result of corrosion through oxidation.#$b#The masonry is tarnished from exposure to lichen and weathering, too. I'd imagine there was a beautiful bronze-and-white style here once.",
    "ami.chat.12": "It's hard to notice the changing of the seasons when you live in the city. Every day is much like the last.#$b#I wouldn't even notice the change in the weather if I didn't change up my wardrobe.#$e#I need to remember to look up from my notes more often..",
    "ami.chat.13": "You can stargaze from Cherry Hill on a clear night.#$b#If you look up high on a summer night, you'll be looking to the billions of stars at the center of our galaxy, owing to our planet's seasonal orbital patterns.#$b#In winter, though, we're pivoted towards the sparse outer reaches of the galaxy, but the stars you see appear brighter due to reduced atmospheric humidity.#$e#.. It's never clear here in winter, though, so I can't test that theory.",
    "ami.chat.14": "Many of the younger trees on the hilltop seem bent and warped from the strong winds. It's a clear indicator of overzealous deforestation.#$b#The older trees were able to grow straight and tall by sheltering eachother, but now each young tree has to survive the elements alone.#$e#It's sad to see the effects of industry, but nature adapts and thrives all the same.",
    "ami.chat.15": "I miss having Mako around.. I never worked on my cooking at school.#$b#Home-eco classes didn't contribute to my exam scores, so it would've been a waste of my time.#$b#In theory, cooking with a wood stove should be very simple. In practice, though..#$e#Rei's cooking? It's ..#$b#Well, she's never been afraid of fire.",
    "ami.chat.16": "*sigh*..#$b#Another year, another kilo more.#$b#.. Oh! @, when'd you get here?",
    "ami.chat.17": "It's lovely being at the shrine and all, so close to the sea, but...#$b#It really is unnerving here. How can you relax in a place like this.. the somber atmosphere of a graveyard.#$b#If I don't stay focused on my studies, my mind wanders to the morbid reality of the shrine.#$e#Rei never seems to give a second thought to tending the graves here. Does she have a deeper connection to the shrine.. or to the dead?",
    "ami.chat.18": "Cooking's nice when you're doing it for fun with friends, but there's only so many times you can burn rice before the novelty wears off.#$b#Why can't making food be half as fun as eating it ..?",
    "ami.chat.19": "It's fun looking at the world around you and finding parallels in mathematics.#$b#Tidal cycles, wind and pressure patterns.. I'm sure you could represent those with simple trigonometry if you tried!#$b#Just imagine the variables that'd go into formulating colours from sunlight refracting through atmospheric hydration in the troposphere. Or for the reaction of solar winds in the magnetosphere!#$e#.. Which part doesn't sound fun?",
    "ami.chat.20": "One of the perks of staying in the valley is having the beach at your doorstep.#$e#There's nothing like drifting in the waves with the water coursing around you.#$b#I could just float around in the sea forever..",
    "ami.chat.21": "...#$e#.. Hi @.#$e#..?",
    "ami.chat.22": "Rainy days are so refreshing.#$b#I can just let loose and feel my problems wash away for a while..",
    "ami.chat.23": "I study full time, so I'm not often able to help out around the shrine.#$b#Maybe you could ask Rei about lending a hand sometime?",
    "ami.chat.24": "(wave 2 1)La la laa~#$b#..?#$e#Hi @.",
    "ami.chat.25": "Cherry Hill is something of a botanical anomaly in the valley these days.#$b#The rush for cheap furniture created a monoculture for hardy, fast-growing timber here. Since the shrine's private land, much of its original biodiversity was preserved.#$b#It's like walking in an ecospheric snowglobe.",
    "ami.chat.26": "I promised Makoto I'd bring back some field notes on coastal flora.#$b#You don't happen to know any interesting specimens, do you?",
    "ami.chat.": "",

    "ami.event.music.0": "You've come at just the right time @, this is my favourite part -- it's Rupìn's Piano Concerto no. 23 in A Major.",
    "ami.event.music.1": "Once, for Mako's birthday, I took her to a recital of Rupìn's Jupiter Overture.#$b#This piece was played first that night. I fell in love when I heard it.",
    "ami.event.music.2": "Even in a major key it's not as joyful, in fact it's a little sad. But the dichotomy between the two made it all the more memorable.",
    "ami.event.music.3": "The Overture makes for a bold, thunderous, emotional performance.. but it's also punctuated with very gentle, delicate movements.#$b#In the opera, it's played in the lovers' duet from the first act.",
    "ami.event.music.4": "Mako missed a lot of the nuance for not having seen the opera, though. She just laughed at the way the composer was dancing around the stage.#$b#I'm not complaining, it was a wonderful night.",
    "ami.event.music.5": "",
    "ami.event.music.6": "",
    "ami.event.music.7": "",
    "ami.event.music.8": "",
    "ami.event.music.9": "",

    "grandpa.test": "DialoguePicker Grandpa default text",
    "grandpa.chat.1": "This place is known as Cherry Hill.#$e#Before that, it was Fire Flower Peak, fer the sun shining through the petals.#$b#Nothing stays the same ferever. Not even a name.",
    "grandpa.chat.2": "Living on a lonely hill has its drawbacks.#$b#Tall steps, bone-chilling winds, knee-high snow...#$b#But it's not a life I'd give up easily.",
    "grandpa.chat.3": "Woods 'round this hill make fer some of the finest timber you'll see in the valley.#$b#We don't just give it away, though. As much as the shrine needs, and nothing more.",
    "grandpa.chat.4": "This Yuuichiro boy is hopeless.#$b#He's been kicking dirt here this many years and I'm still no nearer any great-grandchildren...",
    "grandpa.chat.5": "So you've taken up yer grandpa's farm, eh. It's a good way to be.#$e#Family trades are fading away with modern ways.. when the big stores move in, how can a family compete?#$b#Noone can afford to keep paying more fer less.",
    "grandpa.chat.6": "The old town here was bustling, once upon a time. There was a boom in mining, logging, fishing..#$b#You can only take from nature fer so long before you see consequences.#$e#When the well dries up, so the money does.#$b#They were only here fer the money, so they took it and left us with the scraps.",
    "grandpa.chat.7": "Times change faster than you think.#$b#It feels like only yesterday our Rei was so small, running off fer school each day..#$e#You only get to live each day once, then they're gone.",
    "grandpa.chat.8": "You must be a strong kid after all that work outdoors. Come and help with work on the shrine sometime.#$b#Maybe if you stay around you'll catch my granddaughter's eye! Ho ho ho.",
    "grandpa.chat.9": "If yer looking to swing that axe of yers around here, ferget it.#$b#The trees here are in our hands, and we only take what we need.",
    "grandpa.chat.10": "Before settling into a priest's life, I studied under a master craftsman.#$b#You can study and study all you want to learn the whats and whys, but yer never going to learn how until you go out and work.#$e#Probably best that girl Ami keeps studying before she goes near someone with a scalpel.#$b#I've seen what a fish looks like after she's tried gutting it..",
    "grandpa.chat.11": "I've spent my years as a joiner, a carpenter, even a cooper.#$b#But a roofer? The feller who does our tiles is buried in the hillside!#$b#I'll bet he's watching me now and laughing..",
    "grandpa.chat.12": "*grumble*...#$e#Can't put one foot forward without kicking over one of these blasted flowerpots...",
    "grandpa.chat.13": "(wave 1)*grumble*.. *mumble*...",
    "grandpa.chat.": "",

    "fortune.prompt": "Would you like your fortune told?",
    "fortune.prompt.1": "Cross my palm with silver. Or cash, whichever.",
    "fortune.prompt.2": "Remember to stop by the gift shop on your way out!",

